      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 241,
          "line_end": 242,
          "support": "For each gamma, we obtain b(gamma, L) and c(gamma, L) by fitting the connected correlation weight C(gamma, x) = c(gamma, L) x ln(x) + b(gamma, L) x within different ranges of linear system sizes, x in [8, L]. We use C for the fitting because it can be evaluated for larger system sizes (up to L = 30 in this work), enabling more accurate finite-size scaling."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "readouts": [
    {
      "name": "C",
      "definition": "Connected correlation weight between the left and right partitions, defined as C = sum_{(n,m),(n',m')} |C^LR_{(n,m),(n',m')}(t_s)|^2.",
      "unit": "dimensionless",
      "statistic": "Steady-state value at t_s = 50/J from a single deterministic unitary evolution.",
      "uncertainty": "source_unspecified",
      "resolution": null,
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 193,
          "line_end": 193,
          "support": "We compute the unitary-evolved steady-state bipartite logarithmic fermionic negativity, E = E(C(t_s)) and introduce two additional complementary steady-state quantities: the mutual information, I = S(C^LL(t_s)) + S(C^RR(t_s)) - S(C(t_s)), and the connected correlation weight between the left and right partitions, C = sum_{(n,m),(n',m')} |C^LR_{(n,m),(n',m')}(t_s)|^2."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
